    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-30T03:40:49+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-30T03:40:49+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-29T18:10:49Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-29T18:10:49Z">
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A series of slow moving troughs will move across the state today and Thursday as a couple of cold fronts move across waters to the south. A high pressure system will become established south of the Bight during Friday and persist there on Saturday. A trough will extend from WA over the far west of SA over the weekend.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones. Marine forecasts are also available on VHF and HF radio. View the radio schedule on www.bom.gov.au/marine</text>
                <text type="postamble">Check the latest Coastal Waters Forecasts for information on wind, wave and weather conditions for neighbouring coastal zones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
